@1 = ~Greetings, my good customer. Allow me to introduce myself. I am Vashir al'Maedissir, at your service.~~Greetings, my good lady. Allow me to introduce myself. I am Vashir al'Maedissir, at your service.~
@2 = ~Customer? Am I not your new master?~~Customer? Am I not your new mistress?~
@3 = ~Greetings, Vashir. As for my first wish...~
@4 = ~Ah, no... Yes, I know. My fellow genies imprisoned in bottles, flasks, chests, and other such trinkets pride themselves on granting mortals their wishes. But not all of us, you see. I, for one, prefer honest trade. There is far greater satisfaction in amassing treasure and gold than in simply giving it away. At least, that is what the Caliph always taught me, and I hold his wisdom in the highest regard.~
@5 = ~So, that does not make you my master, but rather one of my many customers. But believe me, you are better off. My wares are truly beautiful, and by not offering you three wishes, I do not impose that foolish limitation of "three" summons.~~So, that does not make you my mistress, but rather one of my many customers. But believe me, you are better off. My wares are truly beautiful, and by not offering you three wishes, I do not impose that foolish limitation of "three" summons.~ //6 & 8 & 9
@6 = ~So I can summon you whenever I like?~
@7 = ~Indeed... provided you don't overdo it. You see, while emerging from this flask is hardly difficult, it does become rather exhausting if I'm summoned too often. So I shall answer your call no more than twice each day. Er... and I'm afraid that point is not open to negotiation.~
@8 = ~Very well. I understand. In that case, show me what you have for sale.~
@9 = ~Very well. Back into your flask with you. I'll call for you again when I have a few gold pieces to spend.~
@10 = ~Now that's more like it. You should know, however, that my inventory is extensive, and I haven't the space to display everything at once. So choose wisely: would you care to browse my magical items, spell scrolls, or potions?~
@11 = ~Greetings, Vashir. Show me the magical items you have for sale, if you please.~
@13 = ~Well then, do try to be more careful next time.~ //EXIT
@14 = ~Greetings, my good customer. Would you care to browse my wares?~~Greetings, my good lady. Would you care to browse my wares?~
@15 = ~Actually, I selected the wrong quick item.~~Actually, I selected the wrong quick item.~
@16 = ~Magical items.~
@17 = ~Spell scrolls.~
@18 = ~Potions.~
@19 = ~Yes. Show me your spell scrolls, if you please.~
@20 = ~That's why I summoned you. Show me the potions you have available, if you please.~
@9901 = ~Battle Axe +3~
@9902 = ~Boomerang Dagger +2~
@9903 = ~Purplethorn +3~
@9904 = ~Staff of Command~
@9905 = ~Staff of the Magi~
@99051 = ~Fireball Lightning~
@9906 = ~Staff of Air +2~
@9907 = ~Staff of Earth +2~
@9908 = ~Staff of Fire +2~
@9909 = ~Scimitar +1~
@99010 = ~Bastard Sword +3~
@99011 = ~Long Sword +3~
@99012 = ~Katana +3~
@99013 = ~Two-Handed Sword +3~